-- title:
--   Integral rescaled exponential for unipotent p^v-torsion, case p=2
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring and $p$ a prime such that $p$ is a non-zero-divisor in $\mathcal O$, with $p=2$; assume $\mathbb Z/p$ is an $\mathcal O$-algebra whose structure map has kernel the ideal $(p)$, and that $\mathcal O$ is $(p)$-adically complete. Let $F$ be a $d$-dimensional commutative formal group law over $\mathcal O$, that is, $d$ power series $F_i$ in the variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,d \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,d$ with vanishing constant term, linear coefficients $\delta_{ij}$ in each of the two blocks, satisfying associativity and commutativity. Let $F_p$ be $d$ power series in the same variables with vanishing constant terms and $\mathrm{coeff}_m(F_{p,i})\cdot p = p^{\deg m}\,\mathrm{coeff}_m(F_i)$ for all $m \neq 0$ (the rescaled law $F(pA,pB)/p$), and let $\varphi$ be $d$ power series in $d$ variables with vanishing constant terms, linear part the identity matrix, and $\varphi_i(F_p) = \varphi_i(A) + \varphi_i(B)$ (a rescaled logarithm). Let $v \ge 1$ and let $R$ be a commutative Hopf $\mathcal O$-algebra, free and finite as an $\mathcal O$-module, with $R$ and $R \otimes_{\mathcal O} R$ both $(p)$-adically complete, together with a surjective $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\pi : \mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_d]] \to R$ such that each $\pi(X_i)$ lies in the radical of $(p)R$, such that $\pi$ is computed by $(p)$-adic evaluation at the points $\pi(X_i)$, such that $\ker \pi$ is generated by the components of the $p^v$-th iterate series of $F$ (defined by $0$ at $0$ and $i \mapsto F_i(\,\cdot\,, X)$ at each successor step), and such that the comultiplication satisfies $\Delta(\pi(X_i)) = F_i(\pi(X)\otimes 1, 1 \otimes \pi(X))$, evaluated $(p)$-adically in $R \otimes_{\mathcal O} R$. Assume finally that the $\mathbb Z/p$-linear dual of $\mathbb Z/p \otimes_{\mathcal O} R$, with its convolution ring structure ([`CartierDual`](def/HopfAlgebra_CartierDual.html#L12)), is a local ring. The conclusion asserts the existence of $d$ power series $\psi_i$ in $d$ variables over $\mathcal O$ with vanishing constant terms, such that for every $N$ and every $i$ all but finitely many coefficients of $\psi_i$ lie in $(p^N)$, and such that $\psi_i(\varphi) = X_i$ and $\varphi_i(\psi) = X_i$ for all $i$.
--
--   This is the $p=2$ case of the statement that, when the Cartier dual of the special fibre of the $p^v$-torsion Hopf algebra is local (unipotence), the inverse $\psi = \varphi^{-1}$ of the rescaled logarithm — the rescaled exponential $f^{-1}(pX)/p$ — not only exists over $\mathcal O$ but has coefficients tending $p$-adically to zero. It is cited by [`MvFormalGroup.exists_rescaledExp_tendsto_zero_of_isLocalRing_cartierDual`](thm.html#MvFormalGroup.exists_rescaledExp_tendsto_zero_of_isLocalRing_cartierDual), which removes the restriction on $p$; the null-sequence property is the integrality input for the logarithm/exponential comparison used in the lifting criterion for finite flat group schemes.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvFormalGroup_exists_rescaledExp_tendsto_zero_of_isLocalRing_cartierDual_of_eq_two.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_HopfAlgebra_CartierDual
import Definitions.Def_MvFormalGroup_BasicV2
